course: dictionary
lesson: 13806
title: Ions: atoms with a charge
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ion is a tiny atom, or a small group of atoms, that has an electric charge. It gets that charge when it gains or loses electrons, which are very small particles.
explain: «Salt breaks up into ions when it dissolves in water.» Ask yourself: is this thing an atom with a charge? If it is, it is an ion. A positive ion has lost electrons, and a negative ion has gained electrons.
explain: «Salty water can carry electricity because it contains ions that can move.» The same idea explains «lithium-ion batteries» in phones and laptops, which store and release power using ions.
fact: An ion is an atom or small group of atoms with an electric charge.
fact: A positive ion has lost electrons.
fact: A negative ion has gained electrons.
fact: «Sodium ion» is one example of an ion, and «positive ion» and «negative ion» are two kinds.
fact: Ions help explain how batteries work and why salty water conducts electricity.
exercise: «Salt breaks into ions when it dissolves in water.» What is an ion? | *An atom or small group of atoms with an electric charge | A kind of drink | A large planet | A type of rock
exercise: A positive ion has lost electrons. What has happened to its electrons? | *Lost electrons | It never had any electrons | Gained more electrons | It turned into water
exercise: «My phone uses a lithium-ion battery.» Copy the word that names the battery type. | *lithium-ion | phone | lithium | battery
test: What does a negative ion have? | Lost its charge | *Gained electrons | Lost electrons | No electrons at all
test: Why can salty water carry electricity? | Because it is sweet | Because it is made of glass | *Because it contains ions that can move | Because it is cold
exam: Which statement about a sodium ion is true? | It has no charge at all | It is always a whole salt crystal | It is a type of battery | *It is an atom with an electric charge
